    {
      "question": "e-612",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
      "old_sha256": "403edfdba4ac70aaba314044b31af01c98956f39409700b3c762bafca74cd7cd",
      "new_sha256": "e1b9df2cd97dae85396ebca4aa6e8d9ebf122f1f3e006231f8ba36eeb8e9e438",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-612",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "Note that \n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(t)=\\int \\mathbf F'(t)\\, \\textrm d t=\\int \\left\\langle 6t^5+2t,\\, \\sec^2 t\\right\\rangle \\, \\textrm d t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \u27e86{t}^{5}+2t,\\,{sec}^{2}\u2061t\u27e9\\,\\text{d}t & =\u27e8\\int (6{t}^{5}+2t)\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int {sec}^{2}\u2061t\\,\\text{d}t\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8{t}^{6}+{t}^{2}+{c}_{1},\\,\\operatorname{tan}\u2061t+{c}_{2}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8{t}^{6}+{t}^{2},\\,\\operatorname{tan}\u2061t\u27e9+\u27e8{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8{t}^{6}+{t}^{2},\\,\\operatorname{tan}\u2061t\u27e9+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf C$ is an arbitrary (vector) constant of integration.",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/example-612.json",
          "file_sha256": "ec683e0e44404b80ace907bb8362259b54d74de85f7391fcfcca3993673ae482"
        }
